# EdgeVerify Project Rules

## What This Project Is

Serverless web app on **Cloudflare Pages + Pages Functions** that displays a visitor's connection info (IP, ISP, VPN/proxy, geolocation) in real time. No database. No logging. No user data persistence.

## Directory Layout

```
EdgeVerify/
├── index.html              # Frontend SPA
├── functions/api/info.js   # Edge function → GET /api/info
├── docs/                   # Architecture, API spec, VPN detection docs
└── spec/                   # Original design spec (Japanese)
```

## Coding Rules

### Backend (`functions/`)
- ES Modules only: `export async function onRequest(context)`
- Runs on the **Cloudflare Workers runtime** (not Node.js — some Node APIs are unavailable)
- `context.request.cf` contains Cloudflare metadata (empty `{}` in local dev)
- Always set fallback values; never let an unhandled error break the response

### Frontend (`index.html`)
- **Vanilla JS only** — no React, Vue, or other frameworks
- **Tailwind CSS via CDN** — do not add a build step
- Fetch `/api/info`, merge with browser-side data (`screen`, `navigator`, WebRTC), then render

### General
- Write comments only when the *why* is non-obvious
- No `console.log` left in production code (use `console.error` for caught exceptions only)
- Do not introduce new npm dependencies without discussion

## Key Constraints

| Item | Constraint |
|------|-----------|
| ip-api.com | HTTP only (free tier), 45 req/min rate limit |
| `cf.isTor` | Non-public Cloudflare property — may be absent |
| `cf.botManagement.score` | Paid Cloudflare plan only |
| Local dev `request.cf` | Always `{}` — all cf fields fall back to defaults |

## Security Non-Negotiables

- Backend must never persist user data (no DB writes, no logging to external services)
- Every response: `Cache-Control: no-store, no-cache, must-revalidate, proxy-revalidate`
- `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *` is intentional (public read-only API)

